1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,880
Don't build with Claude Code until you've installed these

2
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:02,640
five free tools.

3
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:05,060
The first is Context 7, from Upstash.

4
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:08,420
It pulls the current docs for any library you use, so Claude

5
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:10,340
stops writing code that broke two versions ago.

6
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:11,860
Fresh docs every time.

7
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:13,300
The second is Firecrawl.

8
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:14,580
Let's Claude read any website.

9
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:17,620
Docs, blogs, and pricing pages is clean text, so research

10
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:18,740
takes seconds, not hours.

11
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:20,920
The third is the GitHub MCP server.

12
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:24,000
It lets Claude open issues, write the fix, review the pull

13
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,500
request, and merge it so one prompt ships the whole change.

14
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,120
The fourth is Playwright MCP from Microsoft.

15
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:31,860
Click through your login, check out and search like a real

16
00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:34,060
user so every flow is tested before you ship.

17
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:37,840
And the fifth is Chrome DevTools MCP from the Chrome team at

18
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:38,080
Google.

19
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:41,240
It opens your app in a real Chrome, reads the red errors in

20
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:42,640
the console, and fixes them itself.

21
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:45,440
Comment tools, and I'll send you one link with all five.
